      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Lost Valley Trail winds through a narrow canyon to Eden Falls, a 53‑foot cascade of water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansas.com/regions-cities/cities/ponca",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Elk roam the valleys around Ponca, and early morning drives along the river corridor often yield sightings of these majestic animals grazing in fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansas.com/regions-cities/cities/ponca",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ponca hosts the annual 24‑Hours of Horseshoe Hell rock‑climbing festival at Horseshoe Canyon Ranch each September.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansas.com/regions-cities/cities/ponca",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Buffalo National River, established in 1972, flows freely for 135 miles and is one of the few remaining undammed rivers in the lower 48 states.",
